WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:14.246
"Help!" shrieked.

2
00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:18.429
The wind had knocked her down and was whipping her hair over her face.

3
00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:22.311
She was now struggling to hang onto the edge of the chasm.

4
00:00:22.331 --> 00:00:23.832
"Hold on!"

5
00:00:24.052 --> 00:00:28.174
Darb lunged toward her, but he ended up almost falling over the edge himself.

6
00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:31.656
Zing flew overhead, whistling with alarm.

7
00:00:32.412 --> 00:00:36.073
A gust of wind grabbed the dragon, tossing him end over end.

8
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:38.294
"To me!"

9
00:00:38.654 --> 00:00:39.314
Wyssa shouted.

10
00:00:40.134 --> 00:00:43.775
Suddenly Zann felt himself being grabbed by magical energy.

11
00:00:44.535 --> 00:00:47.916
It yanked him backward, away from the terrifying drop-off.

12
00:00:48.656 --> 00:00:51.857
Soon the entire group was safely out of the wind's reach.

13
00:00:51.877 --> 00:00:54.798
"Wow, that was close!"

14
00:00:55.098 --> 00:00:55.938
Perda exclaimed.

15
00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:57.459
Venna nodded.

16
00:00:57.819 --> 00:01:01.760
"No wonder Prince Doni warned us that the Gray Gorge was very dangerous."

17
00:01:02.912 --> 00:01:04.873
Darb stared up at the stone tower.

18
00:01:05.253 --> 00:01:07.154
"That looks like Morb's kind of place."

19
00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:09.254
"Yeah," Zann agreed.

20
00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:11.095
"And my parents are in there!"

21
00:01:11.935 --> 00:01:14.756
His heart pounded at the thought that they might be so close.

22
00:01:15.516 --> 00:01:18.978
After all this time, was he finally going to be with them again?

23
00:01:18.998 --> 00:01:22.119
"How are we going to get in there?"

24
00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:22.939
Gliss wondered.

25
00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:25.980
"Good question," Zann muttered.

26
00:01:26.736 --> 00:01:33.002
The tower was perched halfway across a narrow, ancient-looking stone bridge spanning the Gray Gorge.

27
00:01:33.022 --> 00:01:37.245
"Prince Doni said Morb built this place," Perda said.

28
00:01:37.265 --> 00:01:43.170
"It must have taken a lot of magic to do that, especially in a spot like this."

29
00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:46.613
"Indeed." Wyssa sounded grim.

30
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:51.838
"It seems he must have figured out a new way to steal magic.

31
00:01:52.798 --> 00:01:54.280
Lots of magic."

32
00:01:55.464 --> 00:01:56.744
Zann studied the tower.

33
00:01:57.245 --> 00:02:01.846
"The wind will make it hard to cross the bridge without falling into the gorge," he said.

34
00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:05.287
"But otherwise, it doesn't look that bad.

35
00:02:05.707 --> 00:02:07.587
The gate is small enough to step over."

36
00:02:08.368 --> 00:02:11.489
He pointed to a short gate blocking the entrance to the bridge.

37
00:02:11.509 --> 00:02:15.770
"I suppose it's only meant to keep Roodians out," Venna said.

38
00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.891
"Yeah. Or keep them in," Gliss added.

39
00:02:20.691 --> 00:02:24.608
"I doubt they're thrilled to be Morb's servants."

40
00:02:24.648 --> 00:02:25.749
"So what are we waiting for?"

41
00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:27.669
Perda took a step toward the bridge.

42
00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.770
Wyssa narrowed her eyes.

43
00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.352
"It seems odd that there's no sentry."

44
00:02:33.372 --> 00:02:35.853
"Yes, it does," Venna said.

45
00:02:35.873 --> 00:02:39.655
"I'm sure Morb must have some sort of Shield spell on the place."

46
00:02:40.575 --> 00:02:42.236
"There's only one way to find out.

47
00:02:42.656 --> 00:02:43.076
Come on!"

48
00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:45.397
Zann hurried toward the bridge.

49
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:50.019
Bracing himself against the gusty wind, he stepped over the gate.

50
00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:52.040
Perda was right behind him.

51
00:02:53.328 --> 00:02:55.890
"Wait," Wyssa called from the other side of the gate.

52
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.111
She pointed past Zann.

53
00:02:58.131 --> 00:02:59.011
"What's that?"

54
00:02:59.852 --> 00:03:01.272
Zann peered through the fog.

55
00:03:02.113 --> 00:03:04.354
Something was sitting on the bridge just ahead.

56
00:03:05.134 --> 00:03:06.715
It was small and fluffy.

57
00:03:07.816 --> 00:03:09.157
"Oh!" Zann exclaimed.

58
00:03:09.177 --> 00:03:10.958
"It must be the missing mibbit!"

59
00:03:10.978 --> 00:03:12.979
"Aw, it's cute."

60
00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:14.760
Perda smiled and stepped forward.

61
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.001
"Wait," Zann said.

62
00:03:17.021 --> 00:03:19.282
"It looks kind of tense."

63
00:03:20.222 --> 00:03:21.943
"Here, mibbit, mibbit!"

64
00:03:22.224 --> 00:03:22.804
Perda cooed.

65
00:03:23.572 --> 00:03:24.652
She grabbed for the creature.

66
00:03:25.092 --> 00:03:26.453
It squawked and leaped back.

67
00:03:26.473 --> 00:03:33.155
"Careful, don't panic it or—" Zann gasped as a shock wave of magic energy hit him.

68
00:03:33.755 --> 00:03:35.515
He saw Perda collapse to her knees.

69
00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:40.497
The mibbit was sending out confusing energy waves, just like Vee had described!

70
00:03:41.817 --> 00:03:44.198
Zann had never felt anything like it before.

71
00:03:45.018 --> 00:03:46.818
He couldn't move or think clearly.

72
00:03:47.658 --> 00:03:50.559
Unlike with the scatter beast attack, though, there was no pain.

73
00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:53.100
Still, he felt completely helpless.

74
00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.423
What if Morb looked out a window and spotted him and Perda on the bridge?

75
00:03:58.224 --> 00:03:59.825
He heard moans from behind him.

76
00:04:00.186 --> 00:04:03.849
With great effort he turned his head far enough to see the others.

77
00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.672
Venna was clinging to a tree, gasping for breath.

78
00:04:08.433 --> 00:04:13.057
Gliss was on the ground, helpless—and sliding toward he dizzying drop-off!

79
00:04:14.018 --> 00:04:15.419
Zing wasn't far behind her.

80
00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.461
Zann wanted to save them.

81
00:04:17.822 --> 00:04:18.983
But he still couldn't move.

82
00:04:19.803 --> 00:04:23.907
In fact, he realized he and Perda were dangerously close to the edge too.

83
00:04:24.768 --> 00:04:27.010
He looked for Wyssa, hoping she could help them.

84
00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.852
But she looked just as helpless as the others.

85
00:04:30.913 --> 00:04:34.236
She'd stopped herself from rolling over the edge by clutching the gate.

86
00:04:34.876 --> 00:04:37.138
But Zann could see that her grip was weakening.

87
00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:39.860
Another wave of magic struck them all.

88
00:04:40.621 --> 00:04:43.243
Zann felt himself teetering on the edge of the bridge.

89
00:04:43.644 --> 00:04:46.106
Was this the end for him—for all of them?

90
00:04:46.826 --> 00:04:48.728
Then he saw movement near the gate.

91
00:04:49.396 --> 00:04:53.717
He couldn't turn his head, but he rolled his eyes far enough to see what was happening.

92
00:04:54.718 --> 00:04:55.398
It was Darb!

93
00:04:55.778 --> 00:04:57.558
He was jumping over the small gate.

94
00:04:58.279 --> 00:05:01.339
Dodging Zann and Perda, Darb hurried over to the mibbit.

95
00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.981
"Easy, little fellow," Darb said soothingly.

96
00:05:05.741 --> 00:05:10.702
He gently picked up the mibbit and stroked its ears, just as Vee had taught them.

97
00:05:11.502 --> 00:05:14.183
A moment later the energy waves were gone.

98
00:05:14.203 --> 00:05:19.586
"Whoa!" Perda gasped, sitting up and moving herself away from the drop-off.

99
00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:21.308
Zann did the same.

100
00:05:21.328 --> 00:05:23.309
"Thanks, Darb," he said.

101
00:05:23.329 --> 00:05:26.672
"But why didn't the mibbit's magic affect you?"

102
00:05:27.433 --> 00:05:29.354
Darb shrugged, cuddling the mibbit.

103
00:05:29.655 --> 00:05:32.137
The fluffy creature looked happy and relaxed now.

104
00:05:32.157 --> 00:05:35.339
"Maybe it's because I'm a Void," he said.

105
00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.761
"I don't have any magic for the mibbit to affect."

106
00:05:38.602 --> 00:05:39.322
Wyssa nodded.

107
00:05:39.342 --> 00:05:41.644
"I think you must be right, boy."

108
00:05:42.665 --> 00:05:44.046
Zing flew toward Darb.

109
00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:47.581
He circled him, sniffing at the mibbit curiously.

110
00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:50.443
"Down, boy," Zann told his dragon.

111
00:05:50.463 --> 00:05:52.884
"That mibbit is not a snack!"

112
00:05:53.945 --> 00:05:57.366
Venna brushed the dirt off her clothes and frowned at the mibbit.

113
00:05:57.386 --> 00:06:01.809
"I'm guessing that thing was supposed to be Morb's security guard," she said.

114
00:06:01.829 --> 00:06:03.330
"Shall we proceed?"

115
00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.031
Zann opened his mouth to say yes.

116
00:06:06.692 --> 00:06:11.594
But his words were lost as an eerie howl echoed from the depths of the gorge.

117
00:06:12.675 --> 00:06:14.076
Gliss' eyes widened.

118
00:06:14.548 --> 00:06:16.109
"What was that?"

119
00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:24.054
Before anyone could respond, a huge head on a long, snakelike neck arose from the dark gorge.

120
00:06:25.175 --> 00:06:29.217
The orange glow of its eyes cut through the fog like flames.

121
00:06:30.398 --> 00:06:34.860
With a loud roar, the creature exposed a mouth full of sharp fangs.

122
00:06:35.741 --> 00:06:36.721
Wyssa went pale.

123
00:06:37.222 --> 00:06:39.083
